<title>BELGIUM: AEA airlines' international March RTFKs up 3.8 pct.</title>
<headline>AEA airlines' international March RTFKs up 3.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latest Association of European Airlines (AEA) figures show its members flew 2,191.6 million revenue freight tonne-kilometres (RTFKs) on international routes in March 1997, up 3.8 percent on the same month last year.</p>
<p>The measurement refers to revenue-earning FTKs, derived by multiplying the distance flown by weight of cargo carried.</p>
<p>MARCH 1997</p>
<p>    Region		  Million RTKFs   Pct change on</p>
<p>						    previous year</p>
<p>Geographical Europe	    87.3		 1.2</p>
<p>Europe-N. Africa/M East     103.6		21.3</p>
<p>North Atlantic		  754.8		 0.7</p>
<p>Europe-Far East/Australasia 839.9		 6.7</p>
<p>Europe-Sub Saharan Africa   162.4		-4.9</p>
<p>South Atlantic		  123.3		 0.8</p>
<p>Mid Atlantic		    119.9		 9.9</p>
<p>Total longhaul		2,000.7		 3.2</p>
<p>Total international	 2,191.6		 3.8</p>
<p>*These figures relate to the international scheduled services of AEA member airlines.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
